  "decisions": {
   "text": "﻿Subject,Decision,Reason\r\nSite 17F2M,\"Alternative 3, needs review after changes\",The chain of wetlands gives the largest lift for a cost close to the other alternatives; it is the site's only best buy besides No Action.\r\nSite 17D2E,\"Alternative 1, needs review after changes\",\"Channel removal with a left bank wetland addresses the concrete channel directly, with a large lift and a low unit cost.\"\r\nSite 17B,\"Alternative 2, needs review after changes\",Channel and bank stabilization without beaver removal is the site's best buy and gives the most lift.\r\nSite 2A,\"Alternative 1, needs review after changes\",The largest best buy: the most lift in the watershed at the lowest unit cost.\r\nSite 2B,\"Alternative 1, needs review after changes\",\"The largest best buy, with a low unit cost like Site 2A.\"\r\nSite 3E,\"No Action, needs review after changes\",\"The unit costs of both best buys are far above every other site, so no action is recommended at this site.\"\r\nSite 3F,\"Alternative 1, needs review after changes\",\"The largest best buy, and a place to demonstrate innovative low-cost methods.\"\r\nSite 19A,\"Alternative 2, needs review after changes\",\"The largest best buy, with high lift for South Utoy Creek.\"\r\n\"Final array, P16\",Added,\"Cost-effective plan added: near parity between North and South Utoy, and it introduces the innovative actions at 3F.\"\r\n\"Final array, P9\",Removed,Only one sub-watershed; the study's scope emphasized actions across the whole watershed.\r\n\"Final array, P13\",Removed,Only North Utoy Creek; the first plan with actions in both sub-watersheds is P14.\r\nStep from P1 to P14,Worth it,The smallest acceptable plan: the first with actions in both the North and South Utoy sub-watersheds.\r\nStep from P14 to P16,Worth it,Site 3F adds high benefit at low cost and demonstrates innovative methods for the region.\r\nStep from P16 to P30,Worth it,Site 17B extends actions upstream and cuts sediment delivered to Sites 2A and 2B.\r\nStep from P30 to P62,Worth it,\"Site 17D2E begins to address the concrete channel, a major cause of degradation.\"\r\nTentatively selected plan,\"P128 (National Ecosystem Restoration (NER) plan), to review after changes\",\"All seven sites: the widest geographic coverage, and it directly addresses the concrete channel that drives degradation in the watershed. Sites can still be dropped after further analysis such as real estate.\"\r\n"
  },
